    "12 base colours are binding and must not change without a spec update.",
    "Spec 02 asks for two tints per colour; spec 05 caps the dither palette at 24. Resolution: the five accents that carry most raster light (brass, amber, teal, blue, rust) get a deep tint (45% toward night) and a light tint (45% toward paper); fog gets a light tint (UI-critical: secondary text on slate); phosphor gets a deep tint (dim terminal text). The five neutrals already form their own ramp, olive dithers against night.",
    "quantise is the exact ordered list the palette-lock script (tools/art/palette-lock.mjs) uses. 24 entries.",
    "CSS consumes these through --cf-* custom properties in packages/ui/src/tokens.css; a vitest test keeps the two in sync."
